It's always annoyed me that nethack's "energy recharge" potion was so
rare and so weak. While "confused charging" gives a full mana
recharge, it might be nice to have an alternative method of recharging
mana in late game that doesn't involve confusing oneself.

Why not have a monster (henceforth referred to as a "manasucker")that
drains your mana with each attack, and whose corpse recharges some
energy (maybe d30 or so) upon consumption, much as royal jelly
restores HP? That way, blessed tins of Manasucker would recharge a bit
of energy and a bit of nutrition, something non-hungerless casters
with the Amulet in hand would thoroughly appreciate. Heck, tinned
Manasucker would be a great thing to have on hand while polypiling,
which drains mana and nutrition significantly if done with the spell
rather than the wand.

What's more, if the Manasucker's draining attack were powerful enough,
it would make the decision to genocide R more interesting. For one
thing, if eating a Manasucker while fully charged gave extra spell
points, reverse genocide of Manasuckers might be worthwhile. They'd
also be a monster with a weak physical attack in crowds of Jabberwocks
and other hitty things, much like disenchanters, making them a net
asset. I stopped genociding disenchanters for this reason.

Perhaps Manasuckers could actually be *healed* by attack spells, and
also possess a passive draining attack. I don't know if these
annoyances would significantly affect how casters would  deal with the
creature, though.


